<section class="section"><div class="container narrow">
  <h2>Leadership profile</h2>
  <p>Deepkumar Janardhanan is a <strong>Technology Executive with Marketing Mastery</strong>, with 30+ years across software engineering, solution architecture, program and portfolio management, global delivery, B2B technology marketing, presales, client leadership and business transformation.</p>
  <p>He has held VP-level leadership roles, led distributed organizations of up to 800+ professionals, and managed technology portfolios exceeding $16M. His career includes more than a decade of onsite professional experience in the United States (2001–2012), together with direct client and project experience across the USA, UK, Europe, Gulf / Middle East, Asia, Africa and Australia.</p>
  <p><strong>Current role:</strong> Principal / Delivery Head at Cerebral Ops, where he leads technology, business and delivery strategy across SaaS, ecommerce, cloud, AI and digital-transformation initiatives, while developing positioning, service offerings and go-to-market approaches for technology-led initiatives.</p>

  <h2>Technology leadership</h2>
  <p>Experience spans technology strategy, end-to-end solution architecture, enterprise applications, software development, product engineering, legacy modernization, APIs and integrations, DevOps / CI-CD, AI-enabled transformation, product strategy and technology-business alignment.</p>
  <p>Specific experience includes creating end-to-end technology architecture for a D2C online shop and leading enterprise platforms across insurance, supply chain and digital transformation environments.</p>

  <h2>Marketing & commercial leadership</h2>
  <p>Experience spans B2B technology marketing, GTM strategy, revenue marketing, market positioning and messaging, demand and pipeline generation, product and solution marketing, ABM, sales enablement, account growth, new-logo acquisition, marketing performance, funnel analytics, CRM / marketing automation and sales-and-marketing alignment.</p>

  <h2>Global delivery & delivery economics</h2>
  <p>Experience includes global delivery leadership, delivery operating models, PMO and portfolio governance, delivery methodology, RAID and change control, capacity and utilization planning, forecasting, delivery KPIs, executive governance, stakeholder management, commercial delivery, delivery economics and margin optimization.</p>

  <h2>Transformation & operations</h2>
  <p>Experience spans transformation roadmaps, strategic portfolio prioritization, operating-model redesign, business value, benefits realization, process improvement, organizational scaling, change management, continuous improvement and cross-functional operating leadership.</p>

  <h2>Anticipatory and client-centered leadership</h2>
  <p><strong>I solve problems before they become problems.</strong> I identify technology, delivery and business risks early, establish mitigation strategies before risks become issues, and use executive governance to create predictability.</p>
  <p>I also approach solutions from the client's and user's perspective: understand the underlying business problem, challenge assumptions where useful, analyze requirements in context, and proactively recommend alternatives that improve usability, efficiency and business value.</p>

  <h2>International & industry experience</h2>
  <p><strong>Geographies:</strong> USA · UK · Europe · Gulf / Middle East · Asia · Africa · Australia</p>
  <p><strong>U.S. onsite:</strong> 2001–2012, with direct client and project work in multiple U.S. business environments.</p>
  <p><strong>Industries:</strong> Hedge funds · Retail banking · P&C insurance · Land-title insurance · Retail POS · Supply chain · B2B ecommerce · D2C ecommerce · Government · Telecommunications · Utilities / power · Technology products and services.</p>
  <p><strong>Selected public-sector / infrastructure environments:</strong> U.S. Department of Justice · Commonwealth of Virginia · Governor's Office in Atlanta, Georgia · major power company in Richmond, Virginia · major telecom organization in Tampa, Florida.</p>

  <h2>Education & certifications</h2>
  <p>MBA — NIBM, Chennai (2014), specializing in Technology and Marketing · PMP — PMI (2013) · MCSD — Microsoft (2002) · Bachelor of Commerce — Osmania University (1995)</p>
